    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute turns on whether the trip ran longer than the route shown at booking, and the answer is measured, not argued. The platform's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09112) records 11.5 km against the booked optimal route of 10.0 km (EV-TRIP-09112), an excess of 1.5 km — 15.00% of the optimal distance. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms, and both tests must pass. Here the 1.5 km excess clears the 0.8 km limb but fails the percentage limb (15.00% is below 20%), so no deviation is established on this trip and no distance refund is available under POL-RD-02. The rider's own advocate correctly concedes this gate; the 1.5 km figure the rider quotes is real, but it does not reach the threshold the policy sets. The rider's arithmetic (charged total 19.39 less a recomputed fare of 17.70 = 1.69) is correct in itself, but POL-RD-02 only runs once a deviation is established, so that sum does not become payable, and no amount is refunded.",
    "explanation_continued": "The trace supporting the measurement is unimpaired: EV-GPS-09112 covers 100% of the trip with 133 fixes, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix interval of 0.0 s, so it meets no impairment limb (a)–(c) of POL-RD-07 and no corroboration question arises. The driver's statement that he stayed on ordinary through roads and made no additional stop, and the rider's in-app message that the trip looked a little longer, do not change the measurement — neither identifies a rider-requested detour nor an exculpatory traffic event. The traffic advisory artifact (EV-ADVIS-09112-01) carries no payload and can carry no fact, but since no deviation is established there is nothing for it to excuse. No billing-integrity correction applies under POL-RD-09(4): the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines (tolls_erp 0.00) and no airport surcharge (0.00). No driver compensation arises under POL-RD-04: the distance charged (11.5 km) is not less than the 11.5 km the trace records, so the unbilled-shortfall limb is not met. No repeat-deviation pattern engages POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 610 completed trips in 90 days). No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: trip_id TRP-09112 matches across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, the trace is unimpaired, timestamps are consistent, and every charge line has a counterpart. Outcome: NO_ACTION — the filing party's claim is not supported by the evidence on the threshold test, and the present payment state (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) stands unchanged. The confidence is 0.95, the deciding facts being carried by artifacts at full weight (EV-GPS-09112 and EV-TRIP-09112)."
